{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>According to the word of HaShem they were counted by the hand of Moshe.</b> You will not find in the census of the children of Israel that it mentions among them 'according to the word of HaShem'; but this is mentioned regarding the Levites, to allude to their attribute, which is the attribute of judgment. They were appointed to produce sound, and so the nature of the letter שי״ן is to whistle (לשרוק), and concerning this they said in Sefer Yetzirah: שי״ן whistles, מ״ם is silent (שי״ן שורקת מ״ם דוממת). And besides the appointment for the service of song, he was also appointed over judgment and to guard the Temple, and it was possible for him to slaughter, for the priest did not slaughter, as it is written (Numbers 19:3): ״ושחט אותה לפניו״, and therefore you will find that the verse always mentions regarding the Levites 'according to the word of HaShem,' as it is written (ibid. 3): ״ויפקוד אותם משה על פי ה׳ כאשר צוה״." "<b>And it seems</b> to me to say that therefore the Torah was required to count them from one month and upward, for that is the cycle of the moon, which rules by night; and the attribute of the Levites is the attribute of night, which is called faith (אמונה), and Scripture says (Psalms 92): ״ואמונתך בלילות״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The citation '(שם ג)' refers back to Numbers 3, the same book already cited; the verse quoted is Numbers 3:16 (cf. 3:39)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:34.425484030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}